<title>BELGIUM: Italy EMU deal impossible - Dutch minister Zalm.</title>
<headline>Italy EMU deal impossible - Dutch minister Zalm.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch Finance Minister Gerrit Zalm said on Wednesday that a compromise deal to delay Italy's entry into Monetary Union was not possible and not in line with the EU's Maastricht treaty.</p>
<p>&quot;This kind of deal...that's impossible because it's against the treaty,&quot; Zalm told reporters after speaking to the European Parliament.</p>
<p>He also said countries wishing to join a single currency should strive for sustainable budget deficits below 3.0 percent of GDP.  </p>
<p>&quot;Countries should end up below 3.0 percent (of GDP) and it should be sustainable,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>With regard to a Financial Times article suggesting that Italy will be offered a compromise deal that would delay its entry into EMU until 2000 or 2001, Zalm said &quot;the only guarantee for the Italians is to get their own policy in order.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
